# Rust PR / file checklist

Apply to every Rust change before commit or review. Fix or explicitly justify any deviation in the PR.

## Types and data

- Fixed set of values → `enum`, not `String` / `&str`.
- Strings: literal → `&'static str`, owned → `String`, mixed → `Cow<'static, str>`, shared across threads → `Arc<str>`.
- Unsigned quantities (sizes, token counts, counters) → `u32` / `u64` / `usize`, not `i64`.
- Money → integer minor units (cents, micros) or `rust_decimal`; never `f64`.
- Newtypes for IDs and units: `struct UserId(u64)`, `struct Millis(u64)` — avoid swapped arguments.
- `Option` only where absence is real; do not use `Option` for sentinel defaults.

## Ownership and borrowing

- Function args: `&str` not `&String`, `&[T]` not `&Vec<T>`, `impl AsRef<Path>` for paths.
- No gratuitous `.clone()` / `.to_string()`; each must be justified.
- Struct holding `&'a T`? Prefer owned data or `Arc` unless lifetimes are clearly required.
- Shared mutable state → `Arc<Mutex<T>>` / `RwLock`; hold locks as briefly as possible and never across `.await`.

## Errors

- No `unwrap()` / `expect()` in production code except provably impossible cases (document why).
- Libraries → `thiserror`; application binary → `anyhow` where appropriate.
- Prefer `?` over manual error `match`; add context (`.context("...")`) at boundaries.
- Do not swallow errors silently; `let _ = ...` only when intentional.

## Async

- No blocking in async (`std::fs`, `thread::sleep`, heavy CPU) → `tokio::fs`, `spawn_blocking`.
- Do not hold `std::sync::Mutex` across `.await`.
- Network calls should have timeouts.

## API and structure

- `pub` only for intentional surface; struct fields private by default.
- Derive `Debug` broadly; `Clone` / `PartialEq` / `Serialize` when needed.
- Secrets (tokens, keys) must not appear in `Debug` or logs — custom `Debug` or redacting wrappers.
- Many constructor parameters → builder or config struct.

## Before commit

- `cargo fmt`
- `cargo check`
- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`
- `cargo test`
- No `todo!()`, `dbg!()`, or commented-out dead code.
